{"id": "EUVD-2026-2271", "enisaUuid": "2e0647c9-17a5-30d9-b50c-3bff078c23e1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nInput: lkkbd - disable pending work before freeing device\n\nlkkbd_interrupt() schedules lk->tq via schedule_work(), and the work\nhandler lkkbd_reinit() dereferences the lkkbd structure and its\nserio/input_dev fields.\n\nlkkbd_disconnect() and error paths in lkkbd_connect() free the lkkbd\nstructure without preventing the reinit work from being queued again\nuntil serio_close() returns. This can allow the work handler to run\nafter the structure has been freed, leading to a potential use-after-free.\n\nUse disable_work_sync() instead of cancel_work_sync() to ensure the\nreinit work cannot be re-queued, and call it both in lkkbd_disconnect()\nand in lkkbd_connect() error paths after serio_open().", "datePublished": "2026-01-13T15:31:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:38:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8cf889d45bbc8477206dda78c8f757ea8ff68213", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a7cd1397c209076c371d53bf39a55c138f62342", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cffc4e29b1e2d44ab094cf142d7c461ff09b9104", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e58c88f0cb2d8ed89de78f6f17409d29cfab6c5c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2025-71073", "GHSA-fh34-wp9w-rw28"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0611068b-8e4a-30ac-937d-99eaf3ab3015", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.3"}, {"id": "3056281f-8fed-360a-a381-95f1fa92b9eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <cffc4e29b1e2d44ab094cf142d7c461ff09b9104"}, {"id": "318764f8-956d-3497-ab63-b46f05a1d192", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <3a7cd1397c209076c371d53bf39a55c138f62342"}, {"id": "31a1987c-248a-3a13-a5a6-73b364dec9dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <8cf889d45bbc8477206dda78c8f757ea8ff68213"}, {"id": "62333738-d93b-345d-a6a7-be7d1a976a4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19"}, {"id": "7db83add-2ed3-3052-9f51-9dcf5bcee5eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.64"}, {"id": "b64ad35c-dff9-345d-9166-98cd98ddc074", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "be7b58e5-12f4-3e5e-a4ae-2207cf5170f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <e58c88f0cb2d8ed89de78f6f17409d29cfab6c5c"}, {"id": "e167bb6b-14bb-39a9-98e5-c44253efd33f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f88edeb9-45ef-350b-8c4f-895fd10efe6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1ffbdf5f-15c6-3a6d-a7e2-e8338d019407", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}